From 662dcdd19173a91b9742b5928865a3dc0b2eea6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Wed, 8 Apr 2026 10:31:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/18] fix(rename-prefix): three correctness bugs in repair +
 simple rename

Three independent bugs in `bd rename-prefix` could corrupt a database
during a routine prefix rename. Discovered while migrating gastown rigs
from short two-char prefixes (e.g. `ba`) to project-name prefixes
(e.g. `bastion`):

1. RenameDependencyPrefixInTx used unanchored `LIKE CONCAT(?, '%')` so
   an old prefix that was a substring of another live prefix (e.g. `ba`
   vs `bastion`) matched the target's own dependency rows. Updating
   them with `CONCAT(newPrefix, SUBSTRING(...))` mangled them into
   things like `bastionstion-zbdt.1` and triggered FK violations.
   Fixed by anchoring on the trailing hyphen and adjusting the
   SUBSTRING offset.

2. renamePrefixInDB iterated every issue and unconditionally prepended
   the new prefix, even when the issue's ID already started with the
   target prefix. In a partially-migrated database (e.g. left over
   from a failed earlier rename) this produced double-prefixed IDs
   like `bastion-bastion-foo`. Fixed by skipping rows that don't
   actually carry the old prefix.

3. repairPrefixes always generated content-hash IDs for incorrect
   issues, destroying meaningful suffixes such as `<old>-rig-<rig>`
   and `<old>-witness` that downstream tools (e.g. `gt doctor`)
   expect to find by name. Fixed by trying the semantic mapping
   `<targetPrefix>-<suffix>` first and falling back to a hash only
   when that name is already taken in the rename batch.

Adds three regression tests:
- TestRepairPrefixSubstringCollision (fix 1)
- TestRenamePrefixInDBSkipsAlreadyMigrated (fix 2)
- TestRepairPreservesSemanticSuffix (fix 3)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
